LIFE:

Meeran Syed Mohammed was born on 14th Jamadi-ul-Awal 847 Hijrah (Sept. 9,1443 AD) at Jaunpur which was at that time a famous center of Muslim learning generally called as Shiraz of India. He stands 19th in the lineage of Ali ibn Abutalib and was the second son to his parents. His father besides being a noble of Sharqi Dynasty was a pious man. At the age of 4 Syed Mohammed was taken to the school of Shah Daniyal Chishti, also known as Danial Khizri. Syed Mohammed was gifted with remarkable intelligence and prodigious memory. He memorized the Holy Quran at the age of 7 and completed his studies at the age of 12. The master was so pleased with the scholarly performance of his learned student that he conferred the title of ASAD-UL-ULEMA(A lion of scholars) in the presence of a large gathering of ulemas, nobles and notable personalities of the then Jaunpur. At the age of 18 Meeran Syed Mohammed married his cousin Bibi Allahdadi daughter of Miyan Syed Jalal. The couple was blessed with two sons Miran Syed Mahmood and Miran Syed Ajmal and two daughters Bibi Khonza and Bibi Fatima.